1
00:00:32,657 --> 00:00:33,658
Hey, he's here.

2
00:00:56,639 --> 00:00:58,767
Who are you?

3
00:01:02,103 --> 00:01:03,313
It's been a while.

4
00:01:05,857 --> 00:01:06,858
Emi.

5
00:01:07,817 --> 00:01:09,110
Or should I say...

6
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:11,236
Minamoto Shunsuke.

7
00:01:11,237 --> 00:01:12,322
Ito?

8
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:14,407
Is it you?

9
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:22,791
It's time to rest.

10
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:32,026
THE BLUE ROAD

11
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:36,156
YOUNGMUN FUNERAL HALL

12
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:40,827
It all makes sense now.

13
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:45,915
Your uncle was one of
the serial killer's victims back in '87.

14
00:02:47,792 --> 00:02:49,836
That's why you were so obsessed with this.

15
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:52,881
All of this was just a personal vendetta.

16
00:02:54,424 --> 00:02:57,343
You never actually cared
about any of the other victims.

17
00:02:58,469 --> 00:03:00,053
You were just using this case

18
00:03:00,054 --> 00:03:04,767
to try to finally catch the man who
murdered your uncle all those years ago.

19
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:07,353
Go on, tell me I'm wrong!

20
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:15,195
You think you're a hot shot?

21
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,201
You're a real fucking piece of shit.

22
00:03:24,662 --> 00:03:26,330
Yeah, try me again. Wanna go?

23
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:28,124
You came to my country.
Nobody asked you to.

24
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,794
Hey.

25
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:36,549
Which one of us lost his shit
over Lee Hyeon-seo's death so badly...

26
00:03:37,342 --> 00:03:41,095
that he beat the living daylights
out of the killer? Huh?

27
00:03:41,804 --> 00:03:44,224
And then when I needed you,
you froze up like an idiot.

28
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:47,727
What the hell
are you trying to say, huh?

29
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:50,979
How can you call yourself
a detective? Huh?

30
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:52,065
Hey!

31
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,325
Fuck you!

32
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:17,548
Had enough?

33
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:20,051
You fucker!

34
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:28,268
Take your shot, huh!

35
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:30,728
You motherfucker!

36
00:04:37,568 --> 00:04:38,569
Oh, shit.

37
00:04:44,242 --> 00:04:45,743
You bastard, that hurt!

38
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:49,539
Fuck you!

39
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,259
Kim Seok! Kim Seok!

40
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,678
Listen! Stop!

41
00:05:06,472 --> 00:05:08,182
I get it, I really do.

42
00:05:11,269 --> 00:05:12,562
But at the end of the day

43
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:14,856
your uncle's death

44
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:16,649
and Lee Hyeon-seo's

45
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:18,651
are two separate cases.

46
00:05:20,778 --> 00:05:21,821
You need to accept that.

47
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:28,953
You have to accept it.
It's the only way you'll catch him.

48
00:05:57,023 --> 00:05:59,233
<i>Maybe I got it from my mother...</i>

49
00:06:01,861 --> 00:06:04,822
<i>but I've also heard and seen
strange things all my life.</i>

50
00:06:07,575 --> 00:06:09,369
<i>I still do, to this day.</i>

51
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:14,457
<i>Although,
it wasn't like I had superpowers.</i>

52
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:16,751
<i>It was more like a curse.</i>

53
00:06:18,127 --> 00:06:21,923
<i>My mother tried to suppress this ability
in me by performing a suppression rite.</i>

54
00:06:23,049 --> 00:06:24,467
<i>It hurt. A lot.</i>

55
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:28,638
<i>But I was able to endure it
thanks to Uncle Du-yeong.</i>

56
00:06:56,624 --> 00:06:58,917
Seok! Seok! Don't give in!

57
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:01,253
Stay with me! Keep your eyes open.

58
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:03,214
Don't succumb! Fight it!

59
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:06,884
Seok, look at me.
You can beat it!

60
00:07:09,345 --> 00:07:10,513
Don't be afraid.

61
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:14,350
Seok, it's okay. Stay awake.

62
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:16,686
Seok.

63
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:18,770
Kim Seok!

64
00:07:18,771 --> 00:07:20,397
<i>If it weren't for my Uncle Du-yeong,</i>

65
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:22,275
<i>there's no way</i>
I <i>would have made it through.</i>

66
00:07:25,194 --> 00:07:26,778
<i>That man was like a father to me.</i>

67
00:07:26,779 --> 00:07:28,531
NO ENTRY
INVESTIGATION IN PROGRESS

68
00:07:32,034 --> 00:07:33,744
<i>When I was still a kid...</i>

69
00:07:43,045 --> 00:07:44,797
<i>the uncle who was like a father...</i>

70
00:08:10,823 --> 00:08:12,700
They never found the man who murdered him.

71
00:08:17,538 --> 00:08:20,166
You know, police investigations
were a joke back then.

72
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:25,338
So you decided to become a cop,
and then it happened again.

73
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:28,341
Almost like it's following you.

74
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:34,722
My uncle saved my life,
in more ways than one.

75
00:08:42,146 --> 00:08:43,397
Kinda strange, isn't it?

76
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:47,068
He wasn't even a blood relative.

77
00:08:53,991 --> 00:08:55,451
My daughter...

78
00:08:59,872 --> 00:09:01,165
likes Korea.

79
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:04,377
Uh... BoA.

80
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:09,632
She's a really big fan of Korean music.

81
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:15,263
So, you know,
that's why I tried to learn Korean.

82
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:22,228
It was just so I could talk to Rumi more.

83
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:25,356
Here's the thing, though...

84
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:28,150
She's not my biological daughter.

85
00:09:33,489 --> 00:09:35,575
Rumi's actually my stepdaughter.

86
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:43,082
But I care about her
more than her biological dad does.

87
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:44,584
I'm saying...

88
00:09:45,334 --> 00:09:47,336
whether you're related
by blood or not.

89
00:09:48,129 --> 00:09:49,213
None of that matters.

90
00:09:58,222 --> 00:09:59,223
Hmm.

91
00:10:01,517 --> 00:10:02,517
I'm sorry.

92
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:03,644
Don't worry about it.

93
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:06,396
We solved the case because of you.

94
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:07,857
I might even get a promotion.

95
00:10:08,691 --> 00:10:11,027
As long as I can
stay on top of child support.

96
00:10:12,778 --> 00:10:14,947
Maybe I'll be able to see Rumi
more often too.

97
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:17,240
Well, hey, that's great news.

98
00:10:17,241 --> 00:10:18,326
Mm-hmm.

99
00:10:26,042 --> 00:10:27,043
Cheers.

100
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:42,892
Inose.

101
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:44,894
Mm-hmm.

102
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:46,646
I, uh...

103
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:49,732
I have something to show you.

104
00:11:04,455 --> 00:11:05,456
Whoa...

105
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,749
UNIDENTIFIED BODY IN '30S
FOUND IN SAHA-GU, BUSAN

106
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,293
You collected all of this?

107
00:11:12,463 --> 00:11:13,547
You can see here...

108
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:18,635
The number of killings that were committed
in Korea by this guy, back in '87...

109
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:20,136
FIRST SUSPECTED MURDER
JANUARY 1972

110
00:11:20,137 --> 00:11:22,013
- ...totaled four.
- Right.

111
00:11:22,014 --> 00:11:24,015
SECOND SUSPECTED MURDER
MARCH 1987

112
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:25,767
The last victim was Hong Du-yeong.

113
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:27,268
FOURTH SUSPECTED MURDER:
HONG DU-YEONG

114
00:11:27,269 --> 00:11:28,562
Mm-hmm.

115
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:32,232
Then in 2002,

116
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:34,567
Emi started his rampage
of twisting his victims' limbs

117
00:11:34,568 --> 00:11:35,694
while they were still alive.

118
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:36,986
But...

119
00:11:36,987 --> 00:11:40,700
the victims from '87 didn't have
any hemorrhaging in their pupils.

120
00:11:41,701 --> 00:11:42,993
Which means...

121
00:11:43,744 --> 00:11:44,870
the original killer

122
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:49,750
would twist the limbs
after they were already dead.

123
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:53,211
Let's just assume...

124
00:11:53,212 --> 00:11:54,296
Uh-huh.

125
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:58,550
...Emi learned about the methods
the murderer back then used for his kills.

126
00:11:58,551 --> 00:12:01,512
He copied his techniques, yes,
but also perfected them.

127
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:04,682
One man will know...

128
00:12:05,808 --> 00:12:07,017
those methods.

129
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:11,105
The original?

130
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:14,734
The original...

131
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:21,490
<i>Yeah. The photographer
might know something that could help us.</i>

132
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:26,871
Looks like I'll go
and pay Mikogami a visit.

133
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:30,291
I'm counting on you.

134
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:32,460
Hmm.

135
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:36,922
BREAKING NEWS!
EXCLUSIVE COVERAGE!

136
00:12:38,174 --> 00:12:40,884
Today's scoop comes from
that little country next door, Korea.

137
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:42,051
THE STORY OF
HOW A KILLER IS BORN!

138
00:12:42,052 --> 00:12:44,304
Our story is about
a notorious serial killer,

139
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:47,766
who killed in inventive
and horrific ways across Japan and Korea,

140
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:49,309
and who died during his arrest.

141
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:50,935
What we've heard

142
00:12:50,936 --> 00:12:53,229
is that all this might very well connect

143
00:12:53,230 --> 00:12:57,735
to the fourth largest pharmaceutical titan
in the whole country!

144
00:12:59,111 --> 00:13:00,945
What?

145
00:13:00,946 --> 00:13:03,616
Unfortunately,
neither country is offering any insight

146
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:05,575
on the current investigation,

147
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:09,287
in order to prevent any distraction
from the World Cup right now.

148
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:13,374
<i>Word is that Emi Shunsuke, the killer,
was actually Minamoto Shunsuke,</i>

149
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:16,753
<i>the love child
of the very pharmaceutical titan</i>

150
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:18,464
<i>who hid and denied his own kid!</i>

151
00:13:18,964 --> 00:13:21,591
<i>He's Minamoto Pharmaceutical's
secret child!</i>

152
00:13:21,592 --> 00:13:24,886
It looks like they get intel
faster and in more detail than we do.

153
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:27,973
On top of that,
quite a lot of people watch this show.

154
00:13:28,766 --> 00:13:32,645
I hear Minamoto Pharmaceuticals
has a pretty deep connection to Korea.

155
00:13:33,854 --> 00:13:36,022
Apparently,
Emi Shunsuke's mother is Korean.

156
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:40,110
She was a hostess.
The most popular hostess in the city.

157
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:44,406
Did you hear what he's saying about
the interview that reporter did, though?

158
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:47,618
Something about him killing his pet dog
when he was a kid.

159
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:50,162
If that's true, that's horrible, isn't it?

160
00:13:58,295 --> 00:14:00,840
Hey! You slacking off?

161
00:14:06,428 --> 00:14:08,722
Who says you can watch TV
during work hours?

162
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:10,516
Apologies, sir.

163
00:14:11,433 --> 00:14:12,977
We're finally done with this case.

164
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:15,855
So, where's Inose? Is he ever coming back?

165
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:17,690
I don't know.

166
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:21,443
Oh. I have heard
he booked a flight back to Japan.

167
00:14:23,487 --> 00:14:25,781
What the hell is he thinking now?

168
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:30,244
Chief, if I may...

169
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:34,957
Does this mean
that this case is indeed over?

170
00:14:38,627 --> 00:14:41,546
Foreign Affairs is taking over.
We've done everything we can.

171
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:42,631
Foreign Affairs...

172
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:45,301
So, PSIA?

173
00:14:46,427 --> 00:14:48,721
We have to cooperate,
this can't turn political.

174
00:14:50,514 --> 00:14:52,892
I'm saying
it's not under our jurisdiction anymore.

175
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:11,160
PRIME HOTEL ROOM 1206
LI YOON-OK

176
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,391
You think Korea is your playground?

177
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:37,478
Hmm?

178
00:15:38,062 --> 00:15:39,688
You have no goddamn respect.

179
00:16:09,802 --> 00:16:11,470
Detective Kim Seok is here.

180
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:13,681
Wait outside.

181
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:17,101
Excuse me?

182
00:16:18,435 --> 00:16:19,436
But...

183
00:16:20,688 --> 00:16:21,980
Mr. Seo said I should stay--

184
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:24,441
You know
that I speak on behalf of Mr. Seo.

185
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:25,985
Right?

186
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:39,331
Congratulations on arresting Emi Shunsuke.

187
00:16:39,832 --> 00:16:42,126
Although, he did die, didn't he?

188
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:48,006
Mr. Seo also would like to extend
his gratitude for all of your hard work.

189
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:49,883
I don't care, so just spit it out.

190
00:16:59,101 --> 00:17:00,102
Hmm...

191
00:17:01,562 --> 00:17:05,941
So, you think this case
still isn't over yet, is that right?

192
00:17:07,609 --> 00:17:11,947
Is it true that you believe
there is another killer besides Shunsuke?

193
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:15,034
See, Emi Shunsuke is dead.

194
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:19,413
And the public, well,
they'd rather focus on the World Cup.

195
00:17:20,539 --> 00:17:22,249
Why not just be straightforward?

196
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:27,378
You want me to stop investigating.

197
00:17:27,379 --> 00:17:28,755
ITO MAKOTO,
GODFATHER OF PACHINKO

198
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:30,007
I see you were signing something.

199
00:17:30,758 --> 00:17:33,719
It's pretty pathetic how hard
you guys are trying, I gotta say.

200
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:36,263
What you're doing...

201
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,433
This is a bald-faced threat.

202
00:17:46,356 --> 00:17:48,609
What does that bastard Seo Hyun-tae want?

203
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,654
Are you sure you're ready for this?

204
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:54,156
What?

205
00:17:57,534 --> 00:17:58,535
Will you...

206
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:02,164
stake your life on this investigation?

207
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:04,625
Hmm?

208
00:18:05,709 --> 00:18:07,752
Why don't you go tell
your precious master,

209
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:10,297
that goddamn motherfucker, Mr. Seo...

210
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:15,469
that I wanna see his face, so stop hiding.

211
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:17,888
Do you understand?

212
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:22,559
This is a goddamn joke.

213
00:18:35,697 --> 00:18:36,698
<i>Inose.</i>

214
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:40,327
Seo Hyun-tae's guys
are in Seoul right now.

215
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:42,371
I need you to look into it.

216
00:18:48,877 --> 00:18:49,877
Hello, Professor.

217
00:18:49,878 --> 00:18:52,338
It's Kim Seok,
from the Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency.

218
00:18:52,339 --> 00:18:53,590
We met a while ago.

219
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:55,217
Yes.

220
00:18:56,468 --> 00:18:58,386
Same place we met last time?
See you there.

221
00:18:58,387 --> 00:18:59,471
Is that him?

222
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:05,227
Now he's just ordering me around.

223
00:19:06,186 --> 00:19:07,186
METROPOLITAN POLICE DEPARTMENT

224
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:09,273
Who the hell does he think he is, my boss?

225
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:16,029
Oh, man. I do not wanna be here.

226
00:19:22,369 --> 00:19:23,996
But I did agree to do this properly.

227
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:27,583
Ito's men are in Seoul.

228
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:29,209
Ito...

229
00:19:29,877 --> 00:19:30,877
Ito...

230
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:32,712
- Wait, do you recognize that man?
- Could that be...

231
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:35,548
Is that Inose? I swear it is.
I thought he was in Korea.

232
00:19:35,549 --> 00:19:37,634
- Is he back?
- I mean, I guess he's gotta be.

233
00:19:42,431 --> 00:19:44,724
What the hell were you doing in Korea?

234
00:19:44,725 --> 00:19:46,976
You were ordered back ages ago,
what were you...

235
00:19:46,977 --> 00:19:48,645
What?

236
00:19:49,313 --> 00:19:50,314
Uh...

237
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:53,233
What are Mikogami's visiting hours?

238
00:19:54,651 --> 00:19:57,111
About that. Look, I'm sorry, but that's...

239
00:19:57,112 --> 00:19:59,197
Save your apology.

240
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:01,617
Just secure the visitation. Okay.

241
00:20:21,261 --> 00:20:22,386
What is it?

242
00:20:22,387 --> 00:20:23,972
What's everyone's problem?

243
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:27,434
So... Uh, you see...

244
00:20:28,644 --> 00:20:29,644
INTERROGATION ROOM

245
00:20:29,645 --> 00:20:31,730
There's someone, waiting for you.

246
00:20:41,490 --> 00:20:42,782
Ah, hello!

247
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:44,868
I'm with Internal Affairs.

248
00:20:45,452 --> 00:20:47,037
Uh, Internal Affairs?

249
00:20:47,704 --> 00:20:50,373
I don't have any business
with Internal Affairs.

250
00:20:50,374 --> 00:20:53,125
No, you have business with Mikogami,
isn't that right?

251
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:54,378
- What?
- Well, you did.

252
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:56,712
I'm afraid I have bad news.

253
00:20:56,713 --> 00:20:59,090
Mikogami's execution
was carried out a few days ago,

254
00:20:59,091 --> 00:21:01,259
so I'm afraid any business
with him is concluded.

255
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:02,886
Whoa, hang on. What?

256
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:05,764
Why was it carried out now?

257
00:21:09,142 --> 00:21:10,352
Please have a seat.

258
00:21:12,646 --> 00:21:13,980
What?

259
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:15,482
Go ahead and have a seat.

260
00:21:27,744 --> 00:21:29,788
So, you are an inspector.

261
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:33,417
Your apartment is in Yokohama,
where you currently live alone.

262
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:37,628
But you are still paying quite a large sum
in child support

263
00:21:37,629 --> 00:21:39,631
to your estranged wife, I see.

264
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:43,552
Going to a daughter
who isn't biologically yours.

265
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:49,516
Clearly, you're attached to her.

266
00:21:50,267 --> 00:21:52,686
Even if you're not related by blood.

267
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:56,273
After all, you did help raise her,
did you not?

268
00:21:57,274 --> 00:22:00,527
How come you weren't there for her
her first day of kindergarten?

269
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:05,032
See, a proper father,
would have prioritized it.

270
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:07,159
Hmm.

271
00:22:08,410 --> 00:22:11,245
That's pretty rich,
for you to be talking to me like that.

272
00:22:11,246 --> 00:22:13,957
Do you have kids?
Seems to me, you're not even married yet.

273
00:22:17,169 --> 00:22:18,962
That was a big mistake, you know.

274
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:22,882
I could easily make a complaint.

275
00:22:22,883 --> 00:22:25,719
You're from Internal Affairs.
You already know everything.

276
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:28,429
How my wife and daughter hate me.

277
00:22:28,430 --> 00:22:31,515
I'm probably the least of their concerns,
to be honest with you.

278
00:22:31,516 --> 00:22:34,144
So can you just hurry up
and get this over with?

279
00:22:35,354 --> 00:22:36,355
Well, then.

280
00:22:39,483 --> 00:22:41,568
You know, this whole thing is strange.

281
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:45,988
An internal investigation right
when Emi's case is supposed to reopen.

282
00:22:45,989 --> 00:22:47,074
So...

283
00:22:47,908 --> 00:22:49,326
tell me what's going on.

284
00:22:51,036 --> 00:22:52,036
Huh?

285
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:54,372
BEOLGYO RESTAURANT

286
00:22:54,373 --> 00:22:56,248
Thank you for agreeing to see me,
Professor.

287
00:22:56,249 --> 00:22:57,793
It's my pleasure.

288
00:22:58,418 --> 00:23:01,045
I couldn't stop thinking
about our last conversation,

289
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:02,506
so I did a little more research.

290
00:23:03,548 --> 00:23:04,548
Cheers.

291
00:23:04,549 --> 00:23:05,634
Ah.

292
00:23:13,141 --> 00:23:15,060
So, where did you and I leave off?

293
00:23:16,269 --> 00:23:18,938
Well, I remember
you talked about Emiri's descendants,

294
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:22,067
the Japanese who worshipped Emiri,
elevating him to a god.

295
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:33,703
Well, I'll admit I was hesitant
because it's quite a sensitive subject.

296
00:23:34,788 --> 00:23:38,625
Japan left such a large mark on us
as a country.

297
00:23:40,502 --> 00:23:43,546
I know you already know about
the amount of torture they inflicted,

298
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:46,591
the atrocities, the slaughter,
when they were in Korea.

299
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:49,511
What if I told you
there was a connection to the case?

300
00:23:50,011 --> 00:23:51,012
Right.

301
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:57,227
You mean the limbs were...

302
00:23:57,811 --> 00:23:59,938
Yes. I'm afraid so.

303
00:24:00,689 --> 00:24:03,316
There are records that the
Japanese forces who were deployed here,

304
00:24:04,025 --> 00:24:06,944
broke the limbs of their Korean enemies
as an act of terror.

305
00:24:06,945 --> 00:24:09,322
And this was ordered by the Kwantung Army.

306
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:11,616
The specific unit was Tora.

307
00:24:12,742 --> 00:24:14,661
Doesn't Tora mean the Tiger Unit?

308
00:24:15,495 --> 00:24:18,123
There are also records that,
to prolong the torture...

309
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:21,793
they administered opium to sedate them.

310
00:24:22,377 --> 00:24:25,630
Just like, how Emiri used poppies.

311
00:24:27,132 --> 00:24:28,757
That means that that unit...

312
00:24:28,758 --> 00:24:30,260
Yes, that's right.

313
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:33,763
They may have also
worshipped General Emiri as their god too.

314
00:24:36,808 --> 00:24:39,478
I went to great lengths
to hunt these records down.

315
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:43,023
Here, I scanned them all for you. There.

316
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:44,774
You can see here,

317
00:24:45,817 --> 00:24:47,486
"Founding Principles.

318
00:24:48,528 --> 00:24:51,448
One fear gives birth to endless fears.

319
00:24:52,657 --> 00:24:55,034
But its methods shall remain hidden."

320
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:56,244
TIGER COMMANDER
MINAMOTO HEIHACHI

321
00:24:59,164 --> 00:25:00,540
Oh, one more thing.

322
00:25:01,041 --> 00:25:02,042
Before you go.

323
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:04,084
Remember,

324
00:25:04,085 --> 00:25:07,880
the soldier who naturalized to Korea
with Emiri during the Imjin War,

325
00:25:07,881 --> 00:25:08,965
but then betrayed him?

326
00:25:09,841 --> 00:25:12,928
Yes. I remember you telling me
how he was a spy in the Japanese army.

327
00:25:13,512 --> 00:25:15,764
Well, I found historical evidence
that his name was...

328
00:25:17,516 --> 00:25:18,642
Minamoto.

329
00:25:19,392 --> 00:25:21,185
I know you've heard that name before.

330
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:22,270
Minamoto?

331
00:25:22,771 --> 00:25:25,941
Yes, of Minamoto Pharmaceuticals.

332
00:25:27,317 --> 00:25:29,528
Look here. The commander's name was

333
00:25:30,445 --> 00:25:32,279
Minamoto Heihachi.

334
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:34,741
MINAMOTO HEIHACHI

335
00:25:35,325 --> 00:25:36,660
Now, do you understand?

336
00:25:38,036 --> 00:25:39,913
This means that this man

337
00:25:40,413 --> 00:25:43,290
is a direct ancestor, of Emi Shunsuke,

338
00:25:43,291 --> 00:25:45,210
or rather, shall we say, Minamoto.

339
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:50,631
Oh, also, I have a picture
of Minamoto Heihachi.

340
00:25:50,632 --> 00:25:51,716
It's here somewhere.

341
00:25:53,134 --> 00:25:55,845
Ah. It's this man here.

342
00:26:01,142 --> 00:26:04,895
Minamoto Heihachi never returned to Japan,
even after their defeat.

343
00:26:04,896 --> 00:26:06,272
TIGER UNIT

344
00:26:06,273 --> 00:26:10,485
Instead, he chose to remain in Korea.
He became a Korean.

345
00:26:13,780 --> 00:26:15,115
Thank you for your help again.

346
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:17,909
I'm here anytime.

347
00:26:27,669 --> 00:26:29,129
So... Minamoto.

348
00:26:43,685 --> 00:26:44,853
You can come out now.

349
00:26:53,486 --> 00:26:54,738
I thought it might be you.

350
00:26:56,740 --> 00:26:58,158
How long have you been following me?

351
00:26:59,701 --> 00:27:00,869
Come with me.

352
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:06,332
I'm not one of your lackeys.

353
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:08,500
If Seo Hyun-tae wants to talk,
he can come to me.

354
00:27:08,501 --> 00:27:09,586
This son of a...

355
00:27:15,425 --> 00:27:16,760
You're really pushing it.

356
00:27:24,809 --> 00:27:26,603
Ooh. Whoa.

357
00:27:27,812 --> 00:27:28,897
Nice.

358
00:27:29,564 --> 00:27:30,857
That's a dirty move.

359
00:27:32,317 --> 00:27:33,442
Seriously?

360
00:27:33,443 --> 00:27:36,154
That is way out of line, you prick.

361
00:27:41,951 --> 00:27:42,952
Bring it on.

362
00:27:50,794 --> 00:27:54,463
I was fighting when you were
just a goddamn baby, asshole.

363
00:27:54,464 --> 00:27:55,590
You like that?

364
00:28:07,394 --> 00:28:09,771
Well? You had enough?

365
00:28:13,858 --> 00:28:15,735
What's the real reason you guys came here?

366
00:28:18,446 --> 00:28:19,781
Tell me about Minamoto.

367
00:28:25,829 --> 00:28:27,330
Smug bastard.

368
00:28:33,962 --> 00:28:37,298
Why are you acting so weird?
Come on, what?

369
00:28:37,799 --> 00:28:42,679
Don't tell me the higher-ups,
way above us, knew everything Emi did.

370
00:28:43,805 --> 00:28:46,598
Maybe they really are all
in cahoots with Minamoto, like they say.

371
00:28:46,599 --> 00:28:48,727
This isn't related to the murder case, sorry.

372
00:28:53,022 --> 00:28:54,399
Inspector Inose,

373
00:28:55,024 --> 00:28:58,527
we've received complaints
regarding your neglect of your duty.

374
00:28:58,528 --> 00:29:02,322
Not to mention evidence of embezzlement,
and overstepping your authority.

375
00:29:02,323 --> 00:29:04,199
What the hell are you doing, huh?

376
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:07,161
You're willing to go this far
to stop me from digging?

377
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:09,330
What, is it the pharmaceuticals?

378
00:29:12,459 --> 00:29:13,876
You're way off base, detective.

379
00:29:13,877 --> 00:29:18,423
Have you all forgotten Cindy, Aki,
Yoo I-jin, Lee Hyeon-seo?

380
00:29:21,843 --> 00:29:24,011
Do you realize the number of deaths
that could have been prevented

381
00:29:24,012 --> 00:29:25,722
if you hadn't turned a blind eye?

382
00:29:27,015 --> 00:29:31,144
My goodness.
I had no idea you were this invested.

383
00:29:38,151 --> 00:29:41,196
You do have a knack
for complicating things, don't you?

384
00:29:42,238 --> 00:29:44,491
It's all very simple, you know.

385
00:29:50,413 --> 00:29:52,874
Sit back down, please.

386
00:30:00,799 --> 00:30:02,133
Inspector Inose.

387
00:30:03,843 --> 00:30:07,013
You wanna keep being a good father
to your little girl, don't you?

388
00:30:08,306 --> 00:30:10,015
Because, in that case,

389
00:30:10,016 --> 00:30:13,895
I'd imagine you'd do what it takes to not
get kicked off the force, wouldn't you?

390
00:30:14,479 --> 00:30:16,146
That is one pathetic threat.

391
00:30:16,147 --> 00:30:20,068
Who should come first?
Your family or rather your fanaticism?

392
00:30:23,863 --> 00:30:25,532
But here's the thing...

393
00:30:28,326 --> 00:30:30,161
You don't smell like anything.

394
00:30:36,084 --> 00:30:38,670
And you don't have the mannerisms
of a cop.

395
00:30:39,254 --> 00:30:41,756
What the hell are you doing?

396
00:30:43,591 --> 00:30:45,260
Just checking to see if...

397
00:30:46,719 --> 00:30:48,596
you are who you say you are.

398
00:30:49,973 --> 00:30:52,141
Seo Hyun-tae.

399
00:30:55,770 --> 00:30:56,855
Bingo.

400
00:30:57,814 --> 00:30:59,524
Who are you?

401
00:31:05,405 --> 00:31:09,534
Everyone said you were clever, it's true.

402
00:31:24,883 --> 00:31:26,175
Hello, Yoon Soo-kyung.

403
00:31:26,885 --> 00:31:29,512
From the Republic of Korea
National Intelligence Service.

404
00:31:30,972 --> 00:31:31,973
Hmm.

405
00:31:35,935 --> 00:31:37,395
You mean you're still confused?

406
00:31:38,938 --> 00:31:42,441
Korea is working with Japan
on this issue of national security.

407
00:31:42,442 --> 00:31:44,527
You can think of it that way.

408
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:46,988
This fun for you?

409
00:31:49,741 --> 00:31:50,909
Hmm.

410
00:31:52,994 --> 00:31:54,537
Why don't I cut to the chase?

411
00:31:55,914 --> 00:31:57,749
Wash your hands of this whole mess.

412
00:32:21,773 --> 00:32:23,274
Hey, you're awake.

413
00:32:33,868 --> 00:32:35,119
Where are we?

414
00:32:35,995 --> 00:32:37,330
It's a printing store.

415
00:32:38,581 --> 00:32:41,918
Although it closed down years ago.
No one ever comes here.

416
00:32:42,543 --> 00:32:44,295
You could die here and no one would know.

417
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:47,924
Guess I was on the right track,
given all the fuss you're making.

418
00:32:49,342 --> 00:32:50,343
Yakuza?

419
00:32:50,927 --> 00:32:51,928
That who you are?

420
00:32:52,929 --> 00:32:54,514
Just know, I did warn you.

421
00:32:57,058 --> 00:32:58,935
Focus on surviving instead.

422
00:33:15,243 --> 00:33:16,411
A little bird told me...

423
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:21,332
you wanted to meet me.

424
00:33:35,096 --> 00:33:36,097
What do you think?

425
00:33:37,056 --> 00:33:38,266
Are you Seo Hyun-tae?

426
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:49,318
You see, Mr. Kim,
I'm reporting you as a drug addict.

427
00:33:51,863 --> 00:33:53,322
Better prison than death, no?

428
00:33:59,412 --> 00:34:00,413
Hey!

429
00:34:15,219 --> 00:34:16,262
Hey, Mr. Kim.

430
00:34:23,770 --> 00:34:26,481
Do you want to know
how Hong Du-yeong died?

431
00:34:29,442 --> 00:34:30,943
Or would you rather know why?

432
00:34:33,446 --> 00:34:34,447
Huh?

433
00:34:40,453 --> 00:34:43,081
Don't worry, Mr. Kim. You'll find out.

434
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:02,391
Hey. Don't go too far.

435
00:35:04,435 --> 00:35:05,686
Seo Hyun-tae!

436
00:35:08,523 --> 00:35:09,774
Seo Hyun-tae.

437
00:35:19,367 --> 00:35:20,368
You okay?

438
00:35:22,411 --> 00:35:23,412
Hey, prick.

439
00:35:24,789 --> 00:35:25,790
What?

440
00:35:27,208 --> 00:35:28,709
Go and get Seo Hyun-tae.

441
00:35:31,462 --> 00:35:34,215
I said go get him.

442
00:35:46,018 --> 00:35:47,103
What the fuck?

443
00:35:48,771 --> 00:35:49,772
Get him!

444
00:35:54,944 --> 00:35:56,070
Cocky piece of shit!

445
00:35:56,821 --> 00:35:58,322
Hey, easy now.

446
00:35:58,823 --> 00:36:01,033
- Fuck you!
- Let's not rush things.

447
00:36:02,827 --> 00:36:03,828
Let me.

448
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:55,463
Hey! There he is!

449
00:36:56,422 --> 00:36:57,673
Get him! Now!

450
00:37:21,989 --> 00:37:23,991
Come here, motherfucker!

451
00:38:12,832 --> 00:38:14,041
Go get him! Now!

452
00:38:34,186 --> 00:38:35,396
Goddamn it!

453
00:38:36,355 --> 00:38:37,355
Catch him!

454
00:38:37,356 --> 00:38:39,734
Open the door! You goddamn bitch!

455
00:38:45,281 --> 00:38:46,574
- Break the window!
- Get him!

456
00:38:47,700 --> 00:38:48,701
Come here!

457
00:38:51,912 --> 00:38:53,331
After him! Now!

458
00:39:20,983 --> 00:39:23,069
Inose. Inose.

459
00:39:44,215 --> 00:39:45,758
I'm afraid this isn't over yet.

460
00:39:52,807 --> 00:39:55,351
INCOMING CALL
KIM SEOK

461
00:39:58,312 --> 00:40:01,357
I don't care if you are with the
Korean National Intelligence Service.

462
00:40:02,274 --> 00:40:03,609
Try a warrant next time.

463
00:40:08,572 --> 00:40:09,949
Inose.

464
00:40:21,627 --> 00:40:22,627
Kim Seok?

465
00:40:22,628 --> 00:40:24,880
<i>The person
you are trying to reach is not available.</i>

466
00:40:28,175 --> 00:40:31,512
<i>The person you are trying to reach
is not available. Please leave</i> a <i>message.</i>

467
00:40:33,722 --> 00:40:36,434
Goddamn it! Why?

468
00:40:42,565 --> 00:40:43,566
Shit!

469
00:40:45,151 --> 00:40:46,777
What on earth is going on?

470
00:40:49,488 --> 00:40:50,865
Why?
